900 C1$="David spoke.":C2$="Andrew spoke.":C3$="Martin spoke.":C4$="Alan spoke.":C5$="Susanna spoke."
1000 GOSUB 9000:GOSUB 6100:BM$="And so began their first performance in Germany.":GOSUB 5100
1010 GOSUB 6102:BM$="The crowd was even more excited than it was during their concert in\Italy. The band was getting more and more into it.":GOSUB 5100
1030 GOSUB 6100:BM$="David's energy reached new peaks. Even Martin, the calmest member of\the band, was yelling. The venue was full of excited energy, both above\and below the stage.":GOSUB 5100
1040 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: Forget the ballad, David! Let's keep this energy flowing!":GOSUB 5100
1050 BM$="Alan approached David to talk to him.":GOSUB 5100
1060 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I had the same idea! I'll go tell Andrew!":GOSUB 5100
1070 BM$="Without skipping a beat, David approached Andrew.":GOSUB 5100
1080 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: No way! Things are getting way too hot as it is. We're doing a ballad\next. Go tell Alan!":GOSUB 5100
1090 GOSUB 6100:BM$="Andrew was seemingly the only member to have kept a modicum of sanity,\perhaps due to his sense of responsibility as problem solver of the band.":GOSUB 5100
1100 GOSUB 6101:BM$="The audience left their seats and started crowding the stage. Several\women collapsed and were trampled over.":GOSUB 5100
1110 GOSUB 6100:BM$="The staff pushed the crowd away and helped the women. The concert\continued without any serious injuries.":GOSUB 5100
1120 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6103:BM$="The band played a ballad. The audience returned to their seats. While the\amount of excitement was still high, it was slowly waning.":GOSUB 5100
1130 GOSUB 6099:BM$="Seeing some of their fans collapse seemingly woke up the band members\from their trance, who then used every trick to contain the excitement\of their fans and end the concert without incidents.":GOSUB 5100
1140 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6110:BM$="The band returned to their waiting room, wiping the sweat off their faces.":GOSUB 5100
